<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Reutlingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1377">1377</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Reutlingen was fought on 14 May 1377 outside the imperial city of Reutlingen, where its citizens defeated a force of Count Eberhard II of Württemberg led by his son Ulrich. The victory over Württemberg was a high point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-league">Swabian League</a> of Cities, founded the year before.</p></div>
